    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d584">

                <pb facs="0555" n="547" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg547"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.61331/232: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-11-13T10:00:00+09:00">November 13, 1940—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 14—8:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1143. Peiping’s 430, November 6, 4 p.m., to Department.<anchor n="32"
                        xml:id="d584-f1"/> In view of the Foreign Minister’s expressed desire and
                    intention to obviate <pb facs="0556" n="548" xml:id="pg548"/> as far as
                    practicable interference on the part of Japanese authorities with American
                    rights and interests in China,<anchor n="33" xml:id="d584-f2"/> does the
                    Department wish me to bring to Mr. Matsuoka’s attention either in my next
                    interview or by letter the situation with regard to the China tobacco crop set
                    forth in telegram under reference.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department via Peiping.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department. Repeated to Chungking, Shanghai, Tientsin, Tsingtao.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
